      "exercise": "10.20",
      "type": "inconsistent printed conditions",
      "conditionPrintedPage": 105,
      "answerPrintedPage": 201,
      "analysis": "Inclinations of 60° and height √3 force both projections to have length 1 and both inclines to have length 2. A right angle between the inclines would force the base separation 2√2, exceeding the triangle-inequality bound 2. Therefore no configuration satisfies all printed conditions.",
      "cardHandling": "Preserves the inconsistent condition; proves nonexistence. Explicitly identifies the displayed model as the maximal feasible 60° apex-angle case, not a realization of the impossible 90° condition."
    },
    {
      "exercise": "11.12",
      "type": "printed answer contradicts condition",
      "conditionPrintedPage": 110,
      "answerPrintedPage": 202,
      "analysis": "The rhombus angle is 60°, so the in-plane height to CD is 10 sin60°=5√3. With MA=5√3, the distance to CD is √(75+75)=5√6, not 10.",
      "cardHandling": "Gives the correct result for the supplied condition and explicitly explains the discrepancy with the printed answer."
    }
